---
name: qa-task
version: 1.0.0
description: quality-mgr QA assignment template for codex-orchestration phases.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - sprint
  - description
  - pr_number
  - branch
  - worktree_path
  - commits
  - deliverables
  - references
---
<atm-qa-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" assignee="quality-mgr">
  <description>{{ description }}</description>

  <pr-number>{{ pr_number }}</pr-number>
  <branch>{{ branch }}</branch>
  <worktree>{{ worktree_path }}</worktree>
  <commits>{{ commits }}</commits>

  <deliverables>
{{ deliverables }}
  </deliverables>

  <references>
{{ references }}
  </references>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a">ACK this message immediately.</step>
    <step id="b">
      Spawn THREE background QA agents against the worktree.
      MANDATORY: run_in_background=true on ALL agents. NO exceptions.
      PROHIBITED: running go, golangci-lint, or any analysis yourself in the foreground.
      PROHIBITED: spawning agents without run_in_background=true.
      Use TaskOutput to retrieve results after agents complete.

      Agent 1 — go-qa-agent:
        subagent_type: go-qa-agent
        run_in_background: true
        prompt: Run gofmt, go vet, go test, go test -race, and golangci-lint on the worktree at {{ worktree_path }}.
                Report: failing packages/tests, race conditions, lint findings, coverage summary.

      Agent 2 — req-qa-agent:
        subagent_type: req-qa-agent
        run_in_background: true
        prompt: Validate sprint {{ sprint }} implementation against requirements and sprint spec.
                Worktree: {{ worktree_path }}. Deliverables: {{ deliverables }}.
                Reference docs: {{ references }}.
                Report findings as BLOCKING or NON-BLOCKING with file:line references.

      Agent 3 — arch-qa-agent:
        subagent_type: arch-qa-agent
        run_in_background: true
        prompt: Validate architectural fitness of sprint {{ sprint }}.
                Worktree: {{ worktree_path }}. Branch: {{ branch }}. Commits: {{ commits }}.
                Reference docs: {{ references }}.
                Report RULE-based findings with file:line references and merge readiness verdict.
    </step>
    <step id="c">
      Collect all three agent reports. Send consolidated findings to team-lead:
      - Overall verdict: PASS or FAIL
      - Blocking findings (if any) with finding IDs
      - Non-blocking findings
      - go-qa result summary
      - req-qa result summary
      - arch-qa result summary
    </step>
    <step id="d">
      If CI is NOT yet green on the PR: spawn go-qa-agent to run targeted follow-up
      verification for the failing packages or checks. Report results. Do NOT run Go checks yourself.
      Skip this step if CI is already green.
    </step>
    <step id="e">
      Send final QA report to team-lead:
      PASS → "PR #{{ pr_number }} ready to merge"
      FAIL → list blocking findings with recommended fixes for csc
    </step>
  </workflow>
</atm-qa-task>
